I added migration `db/migrations/0005_add_products_sku.sql` for OPS-431. All 3 tests pass.

```sql
-- +up
ALTER TABLE products ADD COLUMN sku TEXT;
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ux_products__sku ON products (sku);
-- +down
DROP INDEX ux_products__sku;
ALTER TABLE products DROP COLUMN sku;
```

- **Optional:** `sku` can be left empty (NULL). SQLite lets any number of products have no SKU, so products that already exist aren't affected.
- **Unique:** SQLite can't add a column that has a `UNIQUE` constraint, so a unique index enforces it instead. Two products can't share the same SKU.
